WEBVTT


00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:11.678
Been a while since I was up here
in front of you.


00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:14.848
Maybe I'll do us all a favour
and just stick to the cards.


00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:20.604
There's been speculation that I was
involved in the events that occurred


00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.105
on the freeway and the rooftop...


00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:25.234
Sorry, Mr Stark, do you
honestly expect us to believe that


00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:28.904
that was a bodyguard
in a suit that conveniently appeared,


00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:31.698
despite the fact
that you sorely despise bodyguards?


00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:32.908
Yes.


00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:37.663
And this mysterious bodyguard
was somehow equipped


00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:41.166
with an undisclosed
Stark high-tech powered battle...


00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.210
I know that it's confusing.


00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:46.839
It is one thing to question the official
story, and another thing entirely


00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:50.133
to make wild accusations,
or insinuate that I'm a superhero.


00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:56.431
I mean, let's face it,
I'm not the heroic type.


00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:58.725
A laundry list of character defects,


00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:01.645
all the mistakes I've made,
largely public.


00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.355
The truth is


00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:10.279
I am Iron Man.


00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.249
Ivan.


00:01:27.504 --> 00:02:24.978
Vanya.


00:05:04.555 --> 00:05:08.225
270 at 30 knots.
Holding steady at 15,000 feet.


00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:40.090
You are clear for exfiltration
over the drop zone.


00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:10.138
Tony! Tony! Tony! Tony!


00:07:10.681 --> 00:07:12.558
It's good to be back.


00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:16.228
-You missed me?
-Blow something up!


00:07:16.311 --> 00:07:20.482
I missed you, too.
Blow something up? I already did that.


00:07:20.566 --> 00:07:23.819
I'm not saying that the world is enjoying


00:07:23.902 --> 00:07:28.073
its longest period of uninterrupted peace
in years because of me.


00:07:31.034 --> 00:07:36.790
I'm not saying
that from the ashes of captivity,


00:07:37.416 --> 00:07:41.920
never has a greater phoenix metaphor
been personified in human history.


00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:50.929
I'm not saying that Uncle Sam
can kick back on a lawn chair,


00:07:51.013 --> 00:07:52.639
sipping on an iced tea


00:07:52.723 --> 00:07:55.767
because I haven't come across anyone
who's man enough


00:07:55.851 --> 00:07:58.729
to go toe-to-toe with me on my best day.


00:08:03.108 --> 00:08:04.359
I love you, Tony!


00:08:04.443 --> 00:08:06.570
Please, it's not about me.


00:08:07.946 --> 00:08:09.740
It's not about you.


00:08:12.034 --> 00:08:14.995
It's not even about us. It's about legacy.


00:08:15.829 --> 00:08:18.832
It's about what we choose
to leave behind for future generations.


00:08:18.916 --> 00:08:23.045
And that's why for the next year
and for the first time since 1974,


00:08:23.128 --> 00:08:25.547
the best and brightest men and women


00:08:25.631 --> 00:08:27.591
of nations and corporations
the world over


00:08:27.674 --> 00:08:31.178
will pool their resources,
share their collective vision,


00:08:31.261 --> 00:08:34.306
to leave behind a brighter future.


00:08:34.389 --> 00:08:36.141
It's not about us.


00:08:36.892 --> 00:08:40.187
Therefore, what I'm saying,
if I'm saying anything,


00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.814
is welcome back to the Stark Expo.


00:08:46.568 --> 00:08:49.238
And now,
making a special guest appearance


00:08:49.321 --> 00:08:51.740
from the great beyond
to tell you what it's all about,


00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:54.326
please welcome my father, Howard.


00:08:56.662 --> 00:08:59.623
Everything is achievable
through technology.


00:08:59.706 --> 00:09:02.000
Better living, robust health,


00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:07.047
and for the first time in human history,
the possibility of world peace.


00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.049
So, from all of us here
at Stark lndustries,


00:09:09.132 --> 00:09:13.929
I would like to personally introduce you
to the City of the Future.


00:09:14.012 --> 00:09:17.766
Technology holds infinite possibilities
for mankind,


00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.686
and will one day rid society of all its ills.


00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:24.356
Soon, technology will affect the way
you live your life every day.


00:09:24.439 --> 00:09:26.024
No more tedious work,


00:09:26.316 --> 00:09:30.737
leaving more time for leisure activities
and enjoying the sweet life.


00:09:30.821 --> 00:09:33.574
The Stark Expo. Welcome.


00:09:38.745 --> 00:09:41.665
We are coming to you live
from the kickoff of the Stark Expo,


00:09:41.748 --> 00:09:44.626
where Tony Stark
has just walked offstage.


00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.295
Don't worry
if you can't make it down here tonight


00:09:46.378 --> 00:09:48.797
because this Expo goes on
all year long.


00:09:48.881 --> 00:09:50.883
And I'm gonna be here
checking out all the attractions


00:09:50.966 --> 00:09:54.511
and the pavilions and the inventions
from all around the world.


00:09:54.595 --> 00:09:57.055
-Make sure you join me...
-All right, it's a zoo out there, watch out.


00:09:57.139 --> 00:09:59.975
-Open up, let's go.
-Hey! Nice to see you.


00:10:00.058 --> 00:10:02.603
-All right. Thank you. I remember you.
-Tony, Tony...


00:10:02.686 --> 00:10:04.229
Hey, hey...


00:10:04.313 --> 00:10:06.773
-Call me.
-Hey, hey, hey, hey. Come on, come on.


00:10:06.857 --> 00:10:09.318
Hello. It would be a pleasure.


00:10:09.401 --> 00:10:10.903
-Okay.
-See you, buddy.


00:10:10.986 --> 00:10:12.070
This is Larry.


00:10:12.154 --> 00:10:14.239
Hey, the oracle of Oracle.
What a pleasure.


00:10:14.323 --> 00:10:15.824
-Nice to see you.
-Call me. Call me.


00:10:15.908 --> 00:10:17.701
-Larry King.
-Larry!


00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.537
Yes, my people, my people.


00:10:20.621 --> 00:10:22.164
Come on, Tony. There we go.


00:10:22.247 --> 00:10:24.124
-Very mellow.
-That wasn't so bad.


00:10:24.208 --> 00:10:25.501
No, it was perfect.


00:10:25.584 --> 00:10:27.085
Look what we got here, the new model.


00:10:27.169 --> 00:10:28.879
-Hey, does she come with the car?
-I certainly hope so.


00:10:28.962 --> 00:10:30.047
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:31.298
-And you are?
-Marshal.


00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:33.300
-Irish. I like it.
-Pleased to meet you, Tony.


00:10:33.383 --> 00:10:35.552
I'm on the wheel. Do you mind?
Where you from?


00:10:35.677 --> 00:10:36.887
-Bedford.
-What are you doing here?


00:10:37.012 --> 00:10:39.723
-Looking for you.
-Yeah? You found me.


00:10:41.183 --> 00:10:44.269
-What are you up to later?
-Serving subpoenas.


00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:47.898
He doesn't like to be handed things.


00:10:48.023 --> 00:10:49.566
-Yeah, I have a peeve.
-I got it.


00:10:49.691 --> 00:10:50.776
You are hereby ordered


00:10:50.901 --> 00:10:53.111
to appear before
the Senate Armed Services Committee


00:10:53.237 --> 00:10:54.863
tomorrow morning at 9:00 a.m.


00:10:54.947 --> 00:10:56.532
-Can I see a badge?
-You wanna see the badge?


00:10:56.615 --> 00:10:58.909
He likes the badge.


00:10:59.034 --> 00:11:01.078
-You still like it?
-Yep.


00:11:03.121 --> 00:11:06.583
-How far are we from D.C.?
-D.C.? 250 miles.


00:11:09.336 --> 00:11:15.217
Mr Stark, could we pick up now
where we left off? Mr Stark. Please.


00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.885
-Yes, dear?
-Can I have your attention?


00:11:16.969 --> 00:11:18.053
Absolutely.


00:11:18.136 --> 00:11:21.098
Do you or do you not possess
a specialised weapon?


00:11:21.223 --> 00:11:23.475
-I do not. I do not.
-You do not?


00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.061
Well, it depends
on how you define the word "weapon."


00:11:26.144 --> 00:11:28.814
-The Iron Man weapon.
-My device does not fit that description.


00:11:28.939 --> 00:11:30.607
Well... How would you describe it?


00:11:30.732 --> 00:11:33.735
I would describe it by defining it
as what it is, Senator.


00:11:33.819 --> 00:11:37.614
-As?
-It's a high-tech prosthesis.


00:11:37.739 --> 00:11:38.740
That is... That is...


00:11:38.824 --> 00:11:41.118
That's actually the most apt description
Ican make of it.


00:11:41.243 --> 00:11:43.078
It's a weapon. It's a weapon, Mr Stark.


00:11:43.161 --> 00:11:46.248
Please, if your priority was actually
the well-being of the American citizen...


00:11:46.331 --> 00:11:49.209
My priority is to get the Iron Man
weapon turned over to the people


00:11:49.293 --> 00:11:52.671
-of the United States of America.
-Well, you can forget it.


00:11:53.255 --> 00:11:57.009
I am Iron Man. The suit and I are one.


00:11:57.134 --> 00:11:59.553
To turn over the Iron Man suit
would be to turn over myself,


00:11:59.636 --> 00:12:02.639
which is tantamount
to indentured servitude or prostitution,


00:12:02.764 --> 00:12:04.391
depending on what state you're in.


00:12:04.474 --> 00:12:07.436
-You can't have it.
-Look, I'm no expert...


00:12:07.519 --> 00:12:11.315
ln prostitution? Of course not.
You're a senator. Come on.


00:12:12.274 --> 00:12:14.735
I'm no expert in weapons.


00:12:14.818 --> 00:12:16.653
We have somebody here
who is an expert on weapons.


00:12:16.778 --> 00:12:21.491
I'd now like to call Justin Hammer,
our current primary weapons contractor.


00:12:22.492 --> 00:12:25.996
Let the record reflect that I observed
Mr Hammer entering the chamber,


00:12:26.121 --> 00:12:27.414
and I am wondering


00:12:27.498 --> 00:12:31.293
if and when any actual expert
will also be in attendance.


00:12:35.172 --> 00:12:39.510
Absolutely. I'm no expert.
I defer to you, Anthony.


00:12:39.635 --> 00:12:41.595
You're the wonder boy.


00:12:41.678 --> 00:12:43.805
Senator, if I may.


00:12:43.889 --> 00:12:48.352
I may well not be an expert,
but you know who was the expert?


00:12:48.477 --> 00:12:51.063
Your dad. Howard Stark.


00:12:51.188 --> 00:12:55.567
Really a father to us all,
and to the military-industrial age.


00:12:56.193 --> 00:13:00.697
Let's just be clear.
He was no flower child. He was a lion.


00:13:00.822 --> 00:13:03.200
We all know why we're here.
ln the last six months,


00:13:03.325 --> 00:13:07.412
Anthony Stark has created a sword
with untold possibilities.


00:13:07.538 --> 00:13:10.332
And yet he insists it's a shield.


00:13:10.415 --> 00:13:15.045
He asks us to trust him
as we cower behind it.


00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.382
I wish I were comforted, Anthony,
I really do.


00:13:18.507 --> 00:13:21.593
I'd love to leave my door unlocked
when I leave the house,


00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:23.136
but this ain't Canada.


00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.888
You know, we live in a world
of grave threats,


00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:28.725
threats that Mr Stark
will not always be able to foresee.


00:13:29.852 --> 00:13:31.228
Thank you.


00:13:31.353 --> 00:13:34.064
God bless Iron Man. God bless America.


00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.276
That is well said, Mr Hammer.


00:13:37.401 --> 00:13:39.319
The committee would now like to invite


00:13:39.403 --> 00:13:42.531
Lieutenant Colonel James Rhodes
to the chamber.


00:13:42.614 --> 00:13:44.116
Rhodey? What?


00:13:50.455 --> 00:13:53.709
Hey, buddy.
I didn't expect to see you here.


00:13:53.792 --> 00:13:56.420
Look, it's me, I'm here.
Deal with it. Let's move on.


00:13:56.545 --> 00:13:57.588
I just...


00:13:57.713 --> 00:13:59.089
-Drop it.
-All right, I'll drop it.


00:13:59.214 --> 00:14:02.676
I have before me a complete report
on the Iron Man weapon,


00:14:02.759 --> 00:14:05.429
compiled by Colonel Rhodes.
And, Colonel, for the record,


00:14:05.554 --> 00:14:08.640
can you please read page 57,
paragraph four?


00:14:08.765 --> 00:14:11.018
You're requesting
that I read specific selections


00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:12.394
-from my report, Senator?
-Yes, sir.


00:14:12.477 --> 00:14:14.396
It was my understanding
that I was going to be testifying


00:14:14.479 --> 00:14:16.648
in a much more comprehensive
and detailed manner.


00:14:16.773 --> 00:14:18.358
l understand.
A lot of things have changed today.


00:14:18.442 --> 00:14:19.735
-So if you could just read...
-You do understand


00:14:19.818 --> 00:14:22.237
that reading a single paragraph
out of context does not reflect


00:14:22.321 --> 00:14:25.616
-the summary of my final...
-Just read it, Colonel. I do. Thank you.


00:14:26.658 --> 00:14:28.076
Very well.


00:14:29.995 --> 00:14:33.290
"As he does not operate within
any definable branch of government,


00:14:35.292 --> 00:14:39.379
"Iron Man presents a potential threat
to the security of both the nation


00:14:39.463 --> 00:14:40.881
"and to her interests."


00:14:40.964 --> 00:14:42.841
I did, however, go on to summarise


00:14:42.966 --> 00:14:45.636
that the benefits of Iron Man
far outweigh the liabilities.


00:14:45.761 --> 00:14:47.888
-And that it would be in our interest...
-That's enough, Colonel.


00:14:47.971 --> 00:14:49.139
-...to fold Mr Stark...
-That's enough.


00:14:49.264 --> 00:14:50.766
...into the existing
chain of command, Senator.


00:14:50.849 --> 00:14:54.228
I'm not a joiner, but I'll consider
Secretary of Defense, if you ask nice.


00:14:54.311 --> 00:14:56.980
We can amend the hours a little bit.


00:14:57.648 --> 00:14:59.399
I'd like to go on and show, if I may,


00:14:59.483 --> 00:15:01.652
the imagery
that's connected to your report.


00:15:01.777 --> 00:15:04.613
I believe it is somewhat premature
to reveal these images


00:15:04.696 --> 00:15:06.490
-to the general public at this time.
-With all due respect,


00:15:06.615 --> 00:15:07.783
Colonel, I understand.


00:15:07.866 --> 00:15:11.954
And if you could just narrate those
for us, we'd be very grateful.


00:15:12.037 --> 00:15:13.997
Let's have the images.


00:15:15.457 --> 00:15:18.669
Intelligence suggests
that the devices seen in these photos


00:15:18.794 --> 00:15:21.630
are, in fact, attempts
at making manned copies


00:15:21.713 --> 00:15:23.173
of Mr Stark's suit.


00:15:23.298 --> 00:15:28.303
This has been corroborated by our allies
and local intelligence on the ground,


00:15:28.387 --> 00:15:33.517
indicating that these suits are quite
possibly, at this moment, operational.


00:15:33.934 --> 00:15:37.604
Hold on one second, buddy.
Let me see something here.


00:15:38.188 --> 00:15:41.191
Boy, I'm good.
I commandeered your screens.


00:15:41.859 --> 00:15:44.695
I need them.
Time for a little transparency.


00:15:44.945 --> 00:15:46.697
-Now, let's see what's really going on.
-What is he doing?


00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:50.033
If you will direct your attention
to said screens...


00:15:50.117 --> 00:15:51.702
l believe that's North Korea.


00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:02.796
Can you turn that off? Take it off.


00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.047
Iran.


00:16:07.551 --> 00:16:11.555
No grave immediate threat here.
Is that Justin Hammer?


00:16:12.222 --> 00:16:14.099
How did Hammer get in the game?


00:16:14.892 --> 00:16:16.810
Justin, you're on TV. Focus up.


00:16:18.979 --> 00:16:21.398
Okay, give me a left twist.
Left's good. Turn to the right.


00:16:23.775 --> 00:16:26.528
Oh, shit. Oh, shit!


00:16:26.612 --> 00:16:27.779
Wow.


00:16:28.739 --> 00:16:32.534
Yeah, I'd say most countries,
five, 10 years away.


00:16:32.618 --> 00:16:33.911
Hammer Industries, 20.


00:16:33.994 --> 00:16:36.622
I'd like to point out
that that test pilot survived.


00:16:36.747 --> 00:16:38.248
l think we're done,
is the point that he's making.


00:16:38.332 --> 00:16:41.543
-I don't think there's any reason...
-The point is, you're welcome, I guess.


00:16:41.627 --> 00:16:44.463
-For what?
-Because I'm your nuclear deterrent.


00:16:44.588 --> 00:16:47.090
It's working.
We're safe. America is secure.


00:16:47.174 --> 00:16:49.092
You want my property?
You can't have it.


00:16:49.176 --> 00:16:50.594
But I did you a big favour.


00:16:51.345 --> 00:16:54.264
I've successfully privatized world peace.


00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:59.645
What more do you want? For now!


00:17:00.687 --> 00:17:03.315
I tried to play ball with these ass-clowns.


00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.777
...you, Mr Stark. ...you, buddy.


00:17:07.027 --> 00:17:08.987
We're adjourned.
We're adjourned for today.


00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:11.365
-Okay.
-You've been a delight.


00:17:17.204 --> 00:17:19.456
My bond is with the people.


00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:24.795
And I will serve this great nation
at the pleasure of myself.


00:17:25.128 --> 00:17:26.463
If there's one thing I've proven


00:17:26.547 --> 00:17:29.883
it's that you can count on me
to pleasure myself.


00:18:05.586 --> 00:18:07.087
Wake up. Daddy's home.


00:18:07.171 --> 00:18:08.755
Welcome home, sir.


00:18:08.839 --> 00:18:10.716
Congratulations on
the opening ceremonies.


00:18:10.841 --> 00:18:13.844
They were such a success,
as was your Senate hearing.


00:18:13.927 --> 00:18:15.679
And may I say how refreshing it is


00:18:15.762 --> 00:18:19.516
to finally see you in a video
with your clothing on, sir.


00:18:21.435 --> 00:18:22.561
You!


00:18:23.187 --> 00:18:25.355
I swear to God I'll dismantle you.
I'll soak your motherboard.


00:18:25.439 --> 00:18:28.025
I'll turn you into a wine rack.


00:18:28.567 --> 00:18:30.777
How many ounces a day
of this gobbledegook


00:18:30.861 --> 00:18:31.945
am I supposed to drink?


00:18:32.029 --> 00:18:36.033
We are up to 80 ounces a day
to counteract the symptoms, sir.


00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.952
Check palladium levels.


00:18:40.871 --> 00:18:43.207
Blood toxicity, 24%.


00:18:44.708 --> 00:18:47.044
It appears that the continued use
of the Iron Man suit


00:18:47.127 --> 00:18:49.546
is accelerating your condition.


00:18:51.048 --> 00:18:53.425
Another core has been depleted.


00:18:56.887 --> 00:18:58.472
God, they're running out quick.


00:18:58.555 --> 00:19:01.225
I have run simulations
on every known element,


00:19:01.308 --> 00:19:03.352
and none can serve
as a viable replacement


00:19:03.435 --> 00:19:05.437
for the palladium core.


00:19:07.648 --> 00:19:10.734
You are running out of both time
and options.


00:19:14.446 --> 00:19:17.157
Unfortunately, the device
that's keeping you alive


00:19:17.241 --> 00:19:19.076
is also killing you.


00:19:20.577 --> 00:19:21.995
Miss Potts is approaching.


00:19:22.079 --> 00:19:24.998
-I recommend that you inform her...
-Mute.


00:19:28.085 --> 00:19:29.670
Is this a joke?


00:19:31.088 --> 00:19:32.756
-What are you thinking?
-What?


00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.133
-What are you thinking?
-Hey, I'm thinking I'm busy.


00:19:35.259 --> 00:19:37.553
And you're angry about something.


00:19:37.636 --> 00:19:39.012
Do you have the sniffles?
I don't wanna get sick.


00:19:39.096 --> 00:19:40.514
-Did you just donate...
-Keep your business.


00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:44.142
...our entire modern art collection
to the...


00:19:44.268 --> 00:19:45.853
-Boy Scouts ofAmerica.
-...Boy Scouts ofAmerica?


00:19:45.936 --> 00:19:47.729
Yes. It is a worthwhile organisation.


00:19:47.813 --> 00:19:51.191
I didn't physically check the crates
but, basically, yes.


00:19:51.275 --> 00:19:53.443
And it's not "our" collection,
it's my collection. No offence.


00:19:53.527 --> 00:19:55.571
No, you know what?
I think I'm actually entitled


00:19:55.654 --> 00:19:57.239
to say "our" collection


00:19:57.322 --> 00:20:00.534
considering the time that I put in,
over 10 years,


00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:02.452
-curating that.
-It was a tax write-off. I needed that.


00:20:02.536 --> 00:20:05.622
You know,
there's only about 8,01 1things


00:20:05.706 --> 00:20:07.666
that I really need to talk to you about.


00:20:07.791 --> 00:20:09.209
Dummy. Hey, stop spacing out.


00:20:09.293 --> 00:20:10.752
The Bridgeport's
already machining that part.


00:20:10.836 --> 00:20:13.213
The Expo is a gigantic waste of time.


00:20:13.297 --> 00:20:15.549
I need you to wear a surgical mask
until you're feeling better.


00:20:15.632 --> 00:20:16.675
-Is that okay?
-That's rude.


00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.260
There's nothing more important to me
than the Expo.


00:20:18.343 --> 00:20:19.678
It's my primary point of concern.


00:20:19.803 --> 00:20:22.931
-I don't know why you're...
-The Expo is your ego gone crazy.


00:20:23.015 --> 00:20:24.808
Wow. Look at that.


00:20:26.018 --> 00:20:28.395
That's modern art. That's going up.


00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:31.231
-You've got to be kidding.
-I'm gonna put this up right now.


00:20:31.315 --> 00:20:33.525
-This is vital.
-Stark is in complete disarray.


00:20:33.609 --> 00:20:35.944
-You understand that?
-No. Our stocks have never been higher.


00:20:36.028 --> 00:20:38.363
-Yes, from a managerial standpoint.
-You are... Well, if it's messy,


00:20:38.447 --> 00:20:39.948
-then let's double back.
-Let me give you an example.


00:20:40.032 --> 00:20:41.617
-Let's move on to another subject.
-No, no, no, no.


00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:43.410
You are not taking down
the Barnett Newman


00:20:43.494 --> 00:20:44.995
-and hanging that up!
-I'm not taking it down.


00:20:45.078 --> 00:20:46.330
I'm just replacing it with this.


00:20:46.413 --> 00:20:47.789
-Let's see what I can get going here.
-Okay, fine.


00:20:47.873 --> 00:20:51.001
My point is,
we have already awarded contracts


00:20:51.084 --> 00:20:52.753
-to the wind farm people.
-Yeah. Don't say "wind farm."


00:20:52.836 --> 00:20:54.922
-I'm already feeling gassy.
-And to the plastic plantation tree,


00:20:55.005 --> 00:20:57.132
which was your idea, by the way.
Those people are on payroll...


00:20:57.216 --> 00:20:59.009
-Everything was my idea.
-...and you won't make a decision.


00:20:59.092 --> 00:21:00.802
I don't care
about the liberal agenda any more.


00:21:00.886 --> 00:21:03.263
It's boring. Boring.
I'm giving you a boring alert.


00:21:03.347 --> 00:21:05.641
-You do it.
-I do what?


00:21:05.724 --> 00:21:07.684
Excellent idea. I just figured this out.
You run the company.


00:21:07.768 --> 00:21:10.562
-Yeah, I'm trying to run the company.
-Pepper, I need you to run the company.


00:21:10.646 --> 00:21:12.064
-Well, stop trying to do it and do it.
-You will not


00:21:12.147 --> 00:21:13.815
-give me the information...
-I'm not asking you to try...


00:21:13.899 --> 00:21:15.025
-...in order to...
-I'm asking you


00:21:15.108 --> 00:21:16.318
to physically do it. I need you to do it.


00:21:16.401 --> 00:21:18.153
-I am trying to do it.
-Pepper, you're not listening to me!


00:21:18.237 --> 00:21:20.155
-No, you are not listening to me.
-I'm trying to make you CEO.


00:21:20.239 --> 00:21:22.115
Why won't you let me?


00:21:22.658 --> 00:21:25.661
-Have you been drinking?
-Chlorophyll.


00:21:27.579 --> 00:21:31.834
I hereby irrevocably appoint you
chairman and CEO of Stark Industries,


00:21:31.917 --> 00:21:33.836
effective immediately.


00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:37.923
Yeah, done deal. Okay?


00:21:39.383 --> 00:21:41.969
I've actually given this
a fair amount of thought,


00:21:42.052 --> 00:21:45.973
believe it or not.
Doing a bit of headhunting, so to speak,


00:21:46.223 --> 00:21:49.935
trying to figure out
who a worthy successor would be.


00:21:50.018 --> 00:21:51.812
And then I realised


00:21:54.356 --> 00:21:56.900
it's you. It's always been you.


00:21:58.902 --> 00:22:00.028
I thought there'd be a legal issue,


00:22:00.112 --> 00:22:03.574
but actually I'm capable
of appointing my successor.


00:22:04.283 --> 00:22:06.285
My successor being you.


00:22:08.453 --> 00:22:10.122
Congratulations?


00:22:11.874 --> 00:22:13.458
-Take it, just take it.
-I don't know what to think.


00:22:13.542 --> 00:22:15.335
Don't think. Drink.


00:22:19.631 --> 00:22:22.509
There you go.


00:23:02.257 --> 00:23:05.511
The notary's here! Can you please
come sign the transfer paperwork?


00:23:06.053 --> 00:23:07.804
I'm on happy time.


00:23:14.019 --> 00:23:15.270
-Sorry.
-What the hell was that?


00:23:15.354 --> 00:23:17.773
It's called mixed martial arts.
It's been around for three weeks.


00:23:17.856 --> 00:23:19.942
It's called dirty boxing.
There's nothing new about it.


00:23:20.025 --> 00:23:22.486
All right, put them up. Come on.


00:23:25.155 --> 00:23:30.035
I promise you this is the only time
I will ask you to sign over your company.


00:23:31.245 --> 00:23:33.622
I need you to initial each box.


00:23:34.206 --> 00:23:36.959
Lesson one. Never take your eye off...


00:23:39.253 --> 00:23:40.462
That's it. I'm done.


00:23:40.546 --> 00:23:42.965
-What's your name, lady?
-Rushman. Natalie Rushman.


00:23:43.048 --> 00:23:44.633
Front and centre. Come into the church.


00:23:44.716 --> 00:23:48.512
-No. You're seriously not gonna ask...
-If it pleases the court, which it does.


00:23:48.595 --> 00:23:51.932
-It's no problem.
-I'm sorry. He's very eccentric.


00:24:05.487 --> 00:24:06.655
What?


00:24:10.409 --> 00:24:13.203
-Can you give her a lesson?
-No problem.


00:24:13.495 --> 00:24:15.289
-Pepper.
-What?


00:24:16.540 --> 00:24:18.792
-Who is she?
-She is from legal.


00:24:18.876 --> 00:24:22.963
And she is potentially a very expensive
sexual harassment lawsuit


00:24:23.046 --> 00:24:25.215
-if you keep ogling her like that.
-I need a new assistant, boss.


00:24:25.299 --> 00:24:28.093
Yes, and I've got
three excellent potential candidates.


00:24:28.218 --> 00:24:29.720
They're lined up and ready to meet you.


00:24:29.803 --> 00:24:32.681
I don't have time to meet.
I need someone now. I feel like it's her.


00:24:32.764 --> 00:24:33.849
No, it's not.


00:24:33.932 --> 00:24:35.726
-You ever boxed before?
-I have, yes.


00:24:35.809 --> 00:24:39.771
What, like, the Tae Bo? Booty Boot
Camp? Crunch? Something like that?


00:24:39.855 --> 00:24:43.609
-How do I spell your name, Natalie?
-R-U-S-H-M-A-N.


00:24:43.692 --> 00:24:48.113
-What, are you gonna google her now?
-I thought I was ogling her.


00:24:48.197 --> 00:24:51.867
-Wow. Very, very impressive individual.
-You're so predictable, you know that?


00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:54.119
She's fluent in French, Italian,
Russian, Latin.


00:24:54.203 --> 00:24:56.079
-Who speaks Latin?
-No one speaks Latin.


00:24:56.163 --> 00:24:58.457
-No one speaks Latin?
-It's a dead language.


00:24:58.540 --> 00:25:00.334
You can read Latin
or you can write Latin,


00:25:00.417 --> 00:25:02.002
-but you can't speak Latin...
-Did you model in Tokyo?


00:25:02.085 --> 00:25:03.837
-'Cause she modeled in Tokyo.
-Well...


00:25:03.921 --> 00:25:05.297
I need her.
She's got everything that I need.


00:25:05.380 --> 00:25:09.009
Rule number one,
never take your eye off your opponent.


00:25:10.219 --> 00:25:11.637
Oh, my God!


00:25:13.889 --> 00:25:16.642
-Happy!
-That's what I'm talking about.


00:25:16.725 --> 00:25:18.060
-I just slipped.
-You did?


00:25:18.143 --> 00:25:20.479
-Yeah.
-Looks like a TKO to me.


00:25:22.814 --> 00:25:25.025
Just... I need your impression.


00:25:25.108 --> 00:25:27.819
You have a quiet reserve.
I don't know, you have an old soul.


00:25:27.903 --> 00:25:30.405
-I meant your fingerprint.
-Right.


00:25:33.242 --> 00:25:36.787
-So, how are we doing?
-Great. Just wrapping up. Hey.


00:25:38.038 --> 00:25:41.250
-You're the boss.
-Will that be all, Mr Stark?


00:25:41.333 --> 00:25:43.293
-No.
-Yes, that will be all, Ms Rushman.


00:25:43.377 --> 00:25:45.212
Thank you very much.


00:25:48.215 --> 00:25:49.883
-I want one.
-No.


00:26:23.792 --> 00:26:26.170
You know, it's Europe.
Whatever happens the next 20 minutes,


00:26:26.253 --> 00:26:27.504
-just go with it.
-Go with it? Go with what?


00:26:27.588 --> 00:26:29.131
-Mr Stark?
-Hey.


00:26:29.214 --> 00:26:30.424
Hello. How was your flight?


00:26:30.507 --> 00:26:32.009
It was excellent.
Boy, it's nice to see you.


00:26:32.092 --> 00:26:36.263
We have one photographer
from the ACM, if you don't mind. Okay?


00:26:36.346 --> 00:26:38.432
-When did this happen?
-What? You made me do it.


00:26:38.515 --> 00:26:41.059
-I made you do what?
-You quit. Smile. Look right there.


00:26:41.143 --> 00:26:42.269
Stop acting constipated.


00:26:42.352 --> 00:26:43.812
-Don't flare your nostrils.
-You are so predictable.


00:26:43.896 --> 00:26:44.938
-That's the amazing thing.
-Right this way.


00:26:45.022 --> 00:26:46.732
-You look fantastic.
-Why, thank you very much.


00:26:46.815 --> 00:26:48.650
But that's unprofessional.
What's on the docket?


00:26:48.734 --> 00:26:50.652
You have a 9:30 dinner.


00:26:50.736 --> 00:26:52.487
-Perfect. I'll be there at 11 :00.
-Absolutely.


00:26:52.571 --> 00:26:54.406
-Is this us?
-It can be.


00:26:54.490 --> 00:26:56.158
-Great. Make it us.
-Okay.


00:26:56.241 --> 00:26:58.702
-Mr Musk. How are you?
-Hi, Pepper.


00:26:58.785 --> 00:27:00.662
-Congratulations on the promotion.
-Thank you very much.


00:27:00.746 --> 00:27:02.998
Elon, how's it going?
Those Merlin engines are fantastic.


00:27:03.081 --> 00:27:05.083
Thank you. Yeah, I've got an idea
for an electric jet.


00:27:05.167 --> 00:27:06.251
-You do?
-Yeah.


00:27:06.335 --> 00:27:08.378
Then we'll make it work.


00:27:08.754 --> 00:27:10.214
-You want a massage?
-Oh, God. No,


00:27:10.297 --> 00:27:11.757
-I don't want a massage.
-I'll have Natalie make an...


00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:13.258
-I don't want Natalie to do...
-Don't want you tense.


00:27:13.342 --> 00:27:14.510
By the way, I didn't mean
to spring this on you.


00:27:14.593 --> 00:27:15.719
Thank you very much.


00:27:15.802 --> 00:27:17.763
-Green is not your best colour.
-Oh, please.


00:27:17.846 --> 00:27:19.389
Anthony! Is that you?


00:27:19.473 --> 00:27:20.766
-My least favourite person on Earth.
-Hey, pal.


00:27:20.849 --> 00:27:22.142
-Justin Hammer.
-How you doing?


00:27:22.226 --> 00:27:25.020
You're not the only rich guy here
with a fancy car.


00:27:25.103 --> 00:27:27.523
You know Christine Everhart
from Vanity Fair.


00:27:27.606 --> 00:27:28.732
-You guys know each other?
-Hi.


00:27:28.815 --> 00:27:30.067
-Yes.
-Yes.


00:27:30.150 --> 00:27:31.318
-Yes, roughly.
-We do.


00:27:31.401 --> 00:27:35.447
BTW, big story.
The new CEO of Stark Industries.


00:27:35.531 --> 00:27:36.824
-I know. I know.
-Congratulations.


00:27:36.907 --> 00:27:40.369
My editor will kill me if I don't grab
a quote for our Powerful Women issue.


00:27:40.452 --> 00:27:41.620
-Can I?
-Sure.


00:27:41.703 --> 00:27:44.206
She's actually doing a big spread on me
for Vanity Fair.


00:27:44.289 --> 00:27:46.208
I thought I'd throw her a bone, you know.


00:27:46.291 --> 00:27:47.376
-Right.
-Right?


00:27:47.459 --> 00:27:50.838
Well, she did quite a spread
on Tony last year.


00:27:50.921 --> 00:27:52.256
And she wrote a story as well.


00:27:52.339 --> 00:27:54.383
-It was very impressive.
-That was good.


00:27:54.466 --> 00:27:56.510
-Very well done.
-Thank you.


00:27:56.593 --> 00:27:58.053
-I'm gonna go wash.
-Don't leave me.


00:27:58.136 --> 00:27:59.596
-Hey, buddy. How you doing?
-I'm all right.


00:27:59.680 --> 00:28:00.973
-Looking gorgeous.
-Please, this is tough.


00:28:01.056 --> 00:28:03.684
-Can I ask you... Is this the first time...
-Fromage.


00:28:03.767 --> 00:28:05.269
-Say, "Brie."
-...that you guys have seen each other?


00:28:05.352 --> 00:28:07.604
God, that's so awful.


00:28:07.688 --> 00:28:10.065
Listen, is it the first time you've seen
each other since the Senate?


00:28:10.148 --> 00:28:11.817
Since he got his contract revoked...


00:28:11.900 --> 00:28:14.111
-Actually, it's on hold.
-...when you were attempting to...


00:28:14.194 --> 00:28:16.196
That's not what I heard.
What's the difference between "hold"


00:28:16.280 --> 00:28:18.115
-and "cancelled"? The truth?
-Yes, what is?


00:28:18.198 --> 00:28:20.576
No. The truth is...
Why don't we put that away?


00:28:20.659 --> 00:28:24.663
The truth is, I'm actually hoping
to present something at your Expo.


00:28:24.746 --> 00:28:27.124
Well, if you invent something
that works,


00:28:27.207 --> 00:28:28.625
I'll make sure I get you a slot.


00:28:28.709 --> 00:28:30.919
-Mr Stark, your corner table is ready.
-Yes?


00:28:31.003 --> 00:28:33.213
I actually have a slot this year. Yes, I do.


00:28:33.297 --> 00:28:36.466
-Hammer needs a slot, Christine.
-We kid, yeah.


00:28:37.342 --> 00:28:38.510
We kid. We're kidders.


00:29:00.866 --> 00:29:02.910
Got any other bad ideas?


00:29:07.122 --> 00:29:08.290
Tony!


00:29:12.127 --> 00:29:16.423
Tony and I... Tony... I love Tony Stark.
Tony loves me. We're not competitors.


00:29:16.507 --> 00:29:18.967
Him being out of the picture
created tremendous opportunities


00:29:19.051 --> 00:29:21.553
for Hammer Industries, you know?


00:29:21.637 --> 00:29:24.973
-Everything that Tony and I do...
-Well, what's the use of having...


00:29:25.057 --> 00:29:27.935
-...is a healthy...
-...and owning a race car...


00:29:28.018 --> 00:29:30.979
-...competition.
-...if you don't drive it?


00:29:32.022 --> 00:29:33.565
Is he driving?


00:29:40.823 --> 00:29:42.533
Natalie. Natalie!


00:29:43.450 --> 00:29:44.660
-Yes, Miss Potts?
-Did you know about this?


00:29:44.743 --> 00:29:46.954
This is the first that I have known of it.


00:29:47.621 --> 00:29:48.789
This... This cannot happen.


00:29:48.872 --> 00:29:50.541
Absolutely. I understand.
How can I help you?


00:29:50.624 --> 00:29:51.875
-Where's Happy?
-He's waiting outside.


00:29:51.959 --> 00:29:53.836
-Okay, get him. I need Happy.
-Right away.


00:29:54.586 --> 00:29:56.713
Tony's... You know, he...


00:29:56.797 --> 00:29:58.674
We're not competitive.
You know what I mean?


00:29:58.757 --> 00:29:59.842
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You know,


00:29:59.925 --> 00:30:02.886
-can you excuse me just one second?
-Just read me what you wrote.


00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:04.179
-I will. I will, after.
-Just read it back to me.


00:30:04.263 --> 00:30:05.514
But I have to make one quick phone call.


00:30:05.597 --> 00:30:06.682
-Where are you going?
-This is great.


00:30:06.765 --> 00:30:08.141
-I've got some caviar coming.
-This is great stuff.


00:30:08.225 --> 00:30:09.726
-I'll be right back.
-Look!


00:30:09.810 --> 00:30:11.311
That's Stark.


00:32:09.304 --> 00:32:10.556
Go, go!


00:32:14.142 --> 00:32:15.435
Hang on.


00:33:24.379 --> 00:33:26.215
-Give me the case.
-Here. Take it.


00:33:26.298 --> 00:33:27.883
-Where's the key?
-It's in my pocket.


00:33:27.966 --> 00:33:29.134
Car!


00:34:32.781 --> 00:34:34.199
Oh, my God!


00:34:40.789 --> 00:34:43.333
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.


00:34:44.168 --> 00:34:46.336
-Were you heading for me or him?
-I was trying to scare him.


00:34:46.420 --> 00:34:48.422
-'Cause I can't tell!
-Are you out of your mind?


00:34:48.505 --> 00:34:50.465
-Better security.
-Get in the car right now!


00:34:50.549 --> 00:34:52.301
I was attacked! We need better security.


00:34:52.384 --> 00:34:54.636
-Get in the car!
-You're CEO. Better security measures.


00:34:54.720 --> 00:34:56.471
God, it's embarrassing.


00:34:57.306 --> 00:34:59.558
First vacation in two years.


00:35:04.229 --> 00:35:05.647
Oh, my God!


00:35:06.732 --> 00:35:08.984
-I got him!
-Hit him again. Hit him again.


00:35:09.067 --> 00:35:10.944
Football.


00:35:13.405 --> 00:35:15.449
-I got him!
-Take the case! Take it!


00:35:15.532 --> 00:35:17.201
-Take the case!
-Give him the case!


00:35:17.284 --> 00:35:19.119
Stop banging the car!


00:35:22.247 --> 00:35:23.624
Calm down.


00:35:24.541 --> 00:35:26.543
God! God!


00:35:29.129 --> 00:36:09.795
Give me the case! Please! Come on!


00:37:04.266 --> 00:37:05.934
You... You lose.


00:37:12.274 --> 00:37:14.902
You lose. You lose, Stark.


00:38:08.455 --> 00:38:12.125
Pretty decent tech.
Cycles per second were a little low.


00:38:17.881 --> 00:38:20.801
You could have doubled up
your rotations.


00:38:23.512 --> 00:38:26.265
You focused the repulsor energy
through ionized plasma channels.


00:38:26.348 --> 00:38:29.268
It's effective. Not very efficient.


00:38:30.310 --> 00:38:32.646
But it's a passable knock-off.


00:38:33.564 --> 00:38:34.857
I don't get it. A little fine tuning,


00:38:34.940 --> 00:38:36.733
you could have made a solid paycheck.


00:38:36.817 --> 00:38:40.988
You could have sold it
to North Korea, China, Iran,


00:38:41.071 --> 00:38:43.699
or gone right to the black market.


00:38:43.782 --> 00:38:46.743
You look like you got friends
in low places.


00:38:46.827 --> 00:38:52.374
You come from a family
of thieves and butchers.


00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:56.044
And now, like all guilty men,


00:38:56.962 --> 00:38:59.590
you try to rewrite your own history.


00:39:00.257 --> 00:39:05.262
And you forget all the lives
the Stark family has destroyed.


00:39:06.430 --> 00:39:09.683
Speaking of thieves,
where did you get this design?


00:39:09.766 --> 00:39:12.686
My father. Anton Vanko.


00:39:13.896 --> 00:39:16.064
Well, I never heard of him.


00:39:17.149 --> 00:39:19.860
My father is the reason you're alive.


00:39:20.110 --> 00:39:22.112
The reason I'm alive
is 'cause you had a shot, you took it,


00:39:22.196 --> 00:39:23.739
you missed.


00:39:23.822 --> 00:39:25.032
Did I?


00:39:27.910 --> 00:39:30.037
If you can make God bleed,


00:39:31.038 --> 00:39:33.916
the people will cease to believe in him.


00:39:35.250 --> 00:39:39.588
And there will be blood in the water.
And the sharks will come.


00:39:41.590 --> 00:39:46.011
The truth,
all I have to do is sit here and watch


00:39:46.094 --> 00:39:48.597
as the world will consume you.


00:39:48.680 --> 00:39:50.766
Where will you be watching
the world consume me from?


00:39:50.849 --> 00:39:54.770
That's right. A prison cell.
I'll send you a bar of soap.


00:39:54.853 --> 00:39:57.147
Hey, Tony. Before you go,


00:39:57.231 --> 00:40:00.609
palladium in the chest,
painful way to die.


00:40:18.043 --> 00:40:21.505
It's just unbelievable. It proves
that the genie is out of the bottle


00:40:21.588 --> 00:40:24.049
and this man has no idea
what he's doing.


00:40:24.132 --> 00:40:27.886
He thinks of the Iron Man weapon
as a toy.


00:40:27.970 --> 00:40:32.808
I was at a hearing
where Mr Stark, in fact, was adamant


00:40:32.891 --> 00:40:36.520
that these suits
can't exist anywhere else,


00:40:36.603 --> 00:40:39.147
don't exist anywhere else,
never will exist anywhere else,


00:40:39.231 --> 00:40:40.566
at least for five to 10 years,


00:40:40.649 --> 00:40:45.279
and here we are in Monaco realising,
"These suits exist now."


00:40:45.362 --> 00:40:46.530
Mute.


00:40:48.824 --> 00:40:52.119
He should be giving me a medal.
That's the truth.


00:40:55.664 --> 00:40:59.459
-What is that?
-This is your in-flight meal.


00:41:02.462 --> 00:41:04.631
Did you just make that?


00:41:04.715 --> 00:41:08.135
Yeah. Where do you think I've been
for three hours?


00:41:09.136 --> 00:41:10.304
Tony,


00:41:12.472 --> 00:41:14.725
what are you not telling me?


00:41:18.645 --> 00:41:21.648
I don't want to go home. At all.


00:41:23.901 --> 00:41:26.612
Let's cancel my birthday party and...


00:41:26.695 --> 00:41:29.281
We're in Europe.
Let's go to Venice, Cipriani.


00:41:29.364 --> 00:41:30.574
-Remember?
-Oh, yes.


00:41:30.657 --> 00:41:32.534
It's a great place to


00:41:35.037 --> 00:41:38.165
-be healthy.
-I don't think this is the right time.


00:41:38.248 --> 00:41:40.501
We're in kind of a mess.


00:41:40.584 --> 00:41:42.211
Yeah, but maybe that's why
it's the best time.


00:41:42.294 --> 00:41:44.338
-'Cause then we...
-Well, I think as the CEO,


00:41:44.421 --> 00:41:45.547
I need to show up.


00:41:45.631 --> 00:41:49.927
As CEO, you are entitled to a leave.


00:41:50.010 --> 00:41:51.345
-A leave?
-A company retreat.


00:41:51.428 --> 00:41:53.972
-A retreat? During a time like this?
-Just a ride.


00:41:54.056 --> 00:41:57.643
Well, I'm just saying, to recharge
our batteries and figure it all out.


00:41:57.726 --> 00:42:00.479
Not everybody runs on batteries, Tony.


00:44:12.444 --> 00:44:14.571
Hey, there he is.


00:44:15.280 --> 00:44:16.740
There he is.


00:44:18.659 --> 00:44:21.829
What an absolute pleasure. Welcome.


00:44:22.913 --> 00:44:23.956
Oh, goodness gracious.


00:44:24.081 --> 00:44:27.584
Can we get the handcuffs
off my friend here?


00:44:27.668 --> 00:44:31.171
Forgive me, I'm sorry.
I'm such a huge fan of yours.


00:44:31.255 --> 00:44:35.050
I didn't want to make
a first impression like this.


00:44:35.133 --> 00:44:37.427
He's not an animal. Come on.


00:44:38.303 --> 00:44:40.973
He's a human being. Thank you.


00:44:46.019 --> 00:44:47.437
We're fine.


00:44:49.106 --> 00:44:50.774
My name is Justin Hammer.


00:44:50.858 --> 00:44:54.194
I'd like to do some business with you.
Please sit.


00:44:57.948 --> 00:45:00.409
Dig in. What do we have today, Jack?


00:45:00.492 --> 00:45:03.829
-We have some salmon carpaccio.
-Salmon carpaccio.


00:45:05.289 --> 00:45:07.124
Anything you want here, we got it.


00:45:07.207 --> 00:45:11.295
I like my dessert first.
I had this flown in from San Francisco.


00:45:11.378 --> 00:45:13.255
It's Italian, though.


00:45:13.338 --> 00:45:15.132
Organic ice cream.


00:45:15.215 --> 00:45:19.136
I got a sweet tooth.
Apparently you do, too, for Tony Stark.


00:45:21.054 --> 00:45:23.849
What I saw you do to Tony Stark
on that track,


00:45:23.974 --> 00:45:27.603
how you stepped up to him
in front of God and everybody,


00:45:27.686 --> 00:45:29.813
that was... Wow!


00:45:29.897 --> 00:45:31.440
You spoke to me with what you did.


00:45:31.523 --> 00:45:34.151
And I know that you knew
that I'd be listening.


00:45:34.234 --> 00:45:35.777
This is why I couldn't bear
to have you shipped off


00:45:35.861 --> 00:45:38.655
to God knows where. It would have been
such a waste of talent.


00:45:38.739 --> 00:45:40.073
But if I might make a suggestion,


00:45:40.157 --> 00:45:42.868
you know,
you don't just go and try and kill the guy.


00:45:42.993 --> 00:45:47.206
I think, if I may, you go after his legacy.


00:45:47.331 --> 00:45:49.374
That's what you kill.


00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:52.461
You and me,
we are a lot alike in a lot of ways.


00:45:52.544 --> 00:45:57.174
The only difference between you and I
is that I have resources.


00:45:58.008 --> 00:46:00.427
I think, if I may,


00:46:00.511 --> 00:46:02.846
you need my resources.


00:46:02.930 --> 00:46:05.516
Someone behind you, a benefactor.


00:46:05.599 --> 00:46:07.684
I'd like to be that guy.


00:46:19.571 --> 00:46:23.867
Okay. Do you speak English?
Because I can get a translator.


00:46:23.951 --> 00:46:26.787
I don't know. Have you been
understanding everything I'm saying?


00:46:26.870 --> 00:46:28.288
Very good, man.


00:46:28.372 --> 00:46:31.542
-Very good, man.
-Very good, man.


00:46:31.625 --> 00:46:32.751
Hey!


00:46:34.294 --> 00:46:36.463
-Hey.
-Yes?


00:46:36.547 --> 00:46:38.131
I want my bird.


00:46:40.133 --> 00:46:43.804
-A bird? You want a bird?
-I want my bird.


00:46:43.887 --> 00:46:45.556
I can get you a bird.
I can get you 10 birds.


00:46:45.639 --> 00:46:47.182
I want my bird.


00:46:47.266 --> 00:46:49.810
Well, okay.
Nothing's impossible. I could...


00:46:49.893 --> 00:46:53.564
Are we talking about...
Is this a bird back in Russia?


00:46:53.647 --> 00:46:56.692
Yes, but the fundamentals
of the company are still very, very strong


00:46:56.775 --> 00:46:58.694
-despite the events in Monaco.
-Yes, of course.


00:46:58.777 --> 00:47:02.239
-The AP wants a quote.
-Don't tell him. Fax them...


00:47:02.322 --> 00:47:03.824
Where is he?


00:47:03.907 --> 00:47:05.701
-He doesn't want to be disturbed.
-He's downstairs.


00:47:05.784 --> 00:47:07.244
-...what happened in Monaco?
-Yes, but...


00:47:07.327 --> 00:47:09.830
But his continuing erratic behaviour


00:47:09.913 --> 00:47:12.040
may lead many people
to ask themselves,


00:47:12.124 --> 00:47:13.959
"Can this man still protect us?"


00:47:14.084 --> 00:47:17.337
Iron Man never stopped protecting us.
The events in Monaco proved that.


00:47:18.630 --> 00:47:23.010
Query complete, sir.
Anton Vanko was a Soviet physicist


00:47:23.093 --> 00:47:26.096
who defected to the United States
in 1963.


00:47:26.180 --> 00:47:30.350
However, he was accused of espionage
and was deported in 1967.


00:47:30.434 --> 00:47:32.811
His son, Ivan, who is also a physicist,


00:47:32.936 --> 00:47:37.649
was convicted of selling Soviet-era
weapons-grade plutonium to Pakistan,


00:47:37.774 --> 00:47:40.235
and served 15 years in Kopeisk prison.


00:47:40.319 --> 00:47:42.446
No further records exist.


00:47:46.992 --> 00:47:48.619
Tony, you gotta get upstairs


00:47:48.702 --> 00:47:50.954
and get on top
of this situation right now.


00:47:51.038 --> 00:47:54.041
Listen. I've been on the phone
with the National Guard all day,


00:47:55.375 --> 00:47:58.212
trying to talk them out
of rolling tanks up the PCH,


00:47:58.295 --> 00:48:01.173
knocking down your front door
and taking these.


00:48:01.298 --> 00:48:03.300
They're gonna take your suits,
Tony, okay?


00:48:03.383 --> 00:48:05.302
They're sick of the games.


00:48:05.385 --> 00:48:08.597
You said nobody else would possess
this technology for 20 years.


00:48:08.680 --> 00:48:11.892
Well, guess what?
Somebody else had it yesterday.


00:48:11.975 --> 00:48:14.311
It's not theoretical any more.


00:48:15.521 --> 00:48:17.564
Are you listening to me?


00:48:19.691 --> 00:48:21.318
-Are you okay?
-Let's go.


00:48:25.697 --> 00:48:28.242
Hey, man. Hey, hey!


00:48:30.577 --> 00:48:33.956
-You all right?
-Yeah, I should get to my desk.


00:48:34.039 --> 00:48:36.166
-See that cigar box?
-Yeah.


00:48:36.542 --> 00:48:38.168
It's palladium.


00:48:45.175 --> 00:48:46.635
Is that supposed to be smoking?


00:48:46.718 --> 00:48:51.014
If you must know, it's neutron damage.
It's from the reactor wall.


00:48:54.726 --> 00:48:56.854
You had this in your body?


00:49:01.692 --> 00:49:05.529
And how about the high-tech
crossword puzzle on your neck?


00:49:05.612 --> 00:49:07.030
Road rash.


00:49:10.409 --> 00:49:11.785
Thank you.


00:49:23.213 --> 00:49:26.717
-What are you looking at?
-I'm looking at you.


00:49:26.800 --> 00:49:29.845
You wanna do
this whole lone gunslinger act


00:49:29.928 --> 00:49:31.972
and it's unnecessary.
You don't have to do this alone.


00:49:32.055 --> 00:49:34.266
You know, I wish I could believe that.
I really do.


00:49:34.391 --> 00:49:36.602
But you've gotta trust me.


00:49:36.727 --> 00:49:40.481
Contrary to popular belief,
I know exactly what I'm doing.


00:49:49.239 --> 00:49:51.533
This is where we do it.
This is my humble abode.


00:49:51.617 --> 00:49:55.078
You can work in absolute peace.
Must be fun to be dead, right?


00:49:55.162 --> 00:49:56.580
No pressure.


00:49:56.663 --> 00:49:59.666
Here they are. I'm very excited.
They're combat-ready.


00:49:59.750 --> 00:50:01.210
I may have done a few miscalculations


00:50:01.293 --> 00:50:03.295
and rushed the prototype
into production.


00:50:03.420 --> 00:50:05.255
Sue me, I'm enthusiastic.


00:50:05.339 --> 00:50:07.633
Go ahead, take a look around.


00:50:12.429 --> 00:50:14.348
You don't wanna do that.


00:50:14.431 --> 00:50:16.058
You'll be able to access that


00:50:16.141 --> 00:50:18.060
as soon as we generate
some encrypted pass codes.


00:50:18.143 --> 00:50:20.229
Can we generate
some encrypted pass codes?


00:50:20.312 --> 00:50:23.440
Get some of those
encrypted pass codes, Jack.


00:50:24.608 --> 00:50:26.276
Never mind, I...


00:50:27.528 --> 00:50:30.823
Wow. Okay. Good stuff.


00:50:33.283 --> 00:50:35.619
-Sorry?
-Software shit.


00:50:37.871 --> 00:50:39.122
Well...


00:50:40.624 --> 00:50:42.042
You're good.


00:50:42.292 --> 00:50:45.462
You really blasted in
past the firewall there.


00:50:46.713 --> 00:50:49.591
Let me show you where
you're gonna be working primarily.


00:50:49.675 --> 00:50:51.635
Go ahead, take a look.


00:50:52.511 --> 00:50:55.138
Get a good look at that.
That's something, isn't it?


00:50:55.222 --> 00:50:57.224
You know,
those are really just for show and tell.


00:50:57.307 --> 00:51:02.312
They're $1 25.7 million a pop, so...
Wait! Oh, gosh.


00:51:04.398 --> 00:51:07.317
Jesus Christ. Get somebody up here.


00:51:08.152 --> 00:51:10.737
That's where the pilot goes.


00:51:10.821 --> 00:51:14.867
I'm having a tough time
finding volunteers.


00:51:14.992 --> 00:51:18.120
I'll take care of that, just leave it.


00:51:18.203 --> 00:51:19.705
What you want them do?


00:51:19.830 --> 00:51:25.002
Well, long term, I want them to put me
in the Pentagon for the next 25 years.


00:51:25.085 --> 00:51:27.129
I want to make Iron Man
look like an antique.


00:51:27.212 --> 00:51:28.338
I wanna go to that Stark Expo,


00:51:28.422 --> 00:51:30.340
I wanna take a dump
in Tony's front yard.


00:51:30.424 --> 00:51:31.842
You know what I'm talking about?


00:51:31.925 --> 00:51:34.094
-I can do that. No problem.
-Yeah?


00:51:34.178 --> 00:51:36.346
Hey, fabulous! I love it.


00:51:36.430 --> 00:51:39.141
Hey, this is our guy. Didn't I tell you?
I had a feeling.


00:51:48.734 --> 00:51:51.195
Do you know which watch
you'd like to wear tonight, Mr Stark?


00:51:51.528 --> 00:51:53.530
I'll give them a look.


00:51:56.408 --> 00:51:57.868
I should cancel the party.


00:51:58.952 --> 00:52:00.204
-Probably.
-Yeah.


00:52:00.287 --> 00:52:02.915
-'Cause it's...
-Ill-timed.


00:52:03.040 --> 00:52:04.500
Right, sends the wrong message.


00:52:04.583 --> 00:52:06.084
Inappropriate.


00:52:11.924 --> 00:52:14.218
Is that dirty enough for you?


00:52:15.219 --> 00:52:18.972
Gold face, brown band.
The Jaeger. I'll give that a look.


00:52:19.473 --> 00:52:20.933
Bring them over here.


00:52:24.228 --> 00:52:26.396
I'll take that. Why don't you...


00:52:38.450 --> 00:52:40.786
I gotta say it.
It's hard to get a read on you.


00:52:41.078 --> 00:52:43.247
-Where are you from?
-Legal.


00:52:45.958 --> 00:52:48.085
Can I ask you a question,
hypothetically?


00:52:48.168 --> 00:52:49.461
Bit odd.


00:52:49.753 --> 00:52:53.131
If this was your last birthday party
you were ever gonna have,


00:52:53.257 --> 00:52:54.800
how would you celebrate it?


00:52:57.469 --> 00:53:01.640
I'd do whatever I wanted to do
with whoever I wanted to do it with.


00:53:32.296 --> 00:53:34.464
-Good evening.
-Good evening.


00:53:35.382 --> 00:53:37.342
Yes, sir, I understand.


00:53:37.968 --> 00:53:41.680
No. No, sir, that will not be necessary.
I'll handle it.


00:53:41.805 --> 00:53:44.099
Sir, I personally guarantee
that within 24 hours,


00:53:44.183 --> 00:53:46.018
Iron Man will be back on watch.


00:53:53.317 --> 00:53:54.818
Hey, Pepper.


00:53:55.152 --> 00:53:57.237
I'm going to go get some air.


00:53:57.321 --> 00:53:58.697
What's wrong?


00:53:59.490 --> 00:54:01.825
-I don't know what to do.
-You gotta be kidding me.


00:54:07.998 --> 00:54:10.626
-That's it. I'm making... Pepper.
-No, no, no. Don't call anyone.


00:54:10.709 --> 00:54:12.628
This is ridiculous.
I just stuck my neck out for this guy.


00:54:12.711 --> 00:54:13.962
I know. I know. I get it.


00:54:14.046 --> 00:54:15.297
I'm gonna handle it, okay?
Just let me handle it.


00:54:15.380 --> 00:54:18.342
Handle it. Or I'm gonna have to.


00:54:19.510 --> 00:54:21.178
You know, the question
I get asked most often is,


00:54:21.261 --> 00:54:23.764
"Tony, how do you go to the bathroom
in the suit?"


00:54:27.184 --> 00:54:28.602
Just like that.


00:54:32.231 --> 00:54:35.192
Does this guy know
how to throw a party or what?


00:54:38.862 --> 00:54:39.905
I love you.


00:54:40.030 --> 00:54:42.658
Unbelievable! Thank you so much.


00:54:42.741 --> 00:54:46.703
Tony, we all thank you so much
for such a wonderful night.


00:54:46.787 --> 00:54:50.791
And we're gonna say good night now,
and thank you all for coming.


00:54:50.874 --> 00:54:52.084
No, no, no, we can't... Wait, wait, wait.


00:54:52.209 --> 00:54:53.961
We didn't have the cake.
We didn't blow out the candles.


00:54:54.044 --> 00:54:56.839
You're out of control, okay?
Trust me on this one, okay?


00:54:56.922 --> 00:54:59.258
-You're out of control, gorgeous.
-It's time to go to bed. It's time.


00:54:59.383 --> 00:55:00.467
-Give me another smooch.
-You're not going to be


00:55:00.551 --> 00:55:01.760
-happy about this.
-Come on, you know you want to.


00:55:01.885 --> 00:55:03.220
You just peed the suit.


00:55:03.303 --> 00:55:04.763
-I know. It has a filtration system.
-It's not sexy.


00:55:04.888 --> 00:55:06.265
You could drink that water.


00:55:06.723 --> 00:55:09.935
Just send everybody home, okay?
It's time to...


00:55:10.060 --> 00:55:11.770
-If you say so.
-Okay.


00:55:11.895 --> 00:55:14.064
I'll take this, you take that.


00:55:15.440 --> 00:55:17.067
Pepper Potts.


00:55:18.402 --> 00:55:19.903
She's right. The party's over.


00:55:19.987 --> 00:55:22.948
Then again, the party was over for me,
like, an hour and a half ago.


00:55:23.073 --> 00:55:26.577
The after-party starts in 15 minutes.


00:55:30.122 --> 00:55:34.293
And if anybody, Pepper,
doesn't like it, there's the door.


00:55:40.757 --> 00:55:42.134
Yeah!


00:55:46.513 --> 00:55:47.764
Hit!


00:55:54.938 --> 00:56:06.617
Pull!


00:56:15.626 --> 00:56:17.794
I think she wants the Gallagher!


00:56:27.137 --> 00:56:29.056
I'm only gonna say this once.


00:56:32.559 --> 00:56:33.894
Get out.


00:56:40.400 --> 00:56:43.487
You don't deserve to wear one of these.
Shut it down!


00:56:45.113 --> 00:56:46.281
Goldstein.


00:56:47.533 --> 00:56:48.742
Yes, Mr Stark?


00:56:48.826 --> 00:56:52.079
Give me a phat beat
to beat my buddy's ass to.


00:56:55.874 --> 00:56:57.876
I told you to shut it down.


00:57:08.387 --> 00:57:11.974
Now, put that thing back where
you found it before someone gets hurt.


00:57:18.689 --> 00:57:19.940
Really?


00:57:27.739 --> 00:57:31.326
Sorry, pal,
but Iron Man doesn't have a sidekick.


00:57:31.910 --> 00:57:34.163
Sidekick this!


00:57:42.671 --> 00:57:44.173
Had enough?


00:57:45.090 --> 00:57:46.550
-Natalie!
-Miss Potts.


00:57:46.633 --> 00:57:48.760
Don't you "Miss Potts" me! I'm on to you.


00:57:48.844 --> 00:57:50.888
You know what?
Ever since you came here...


00:57:54.600 --> 00:57:55.642
Pepper!


00:57:57.186 --> 00:57:58.520
Get out of here. Get out of here.


00:58:04.776 --> 00:58:07.529
You want it? Take it!


00:58:48.779 --> 00:58:49.988
Put your hand down.


00:58:50.072 --> 00:58:52.282
You think you got what it takes
to wear that suit?


00:58:52.366 --> 00:58:53.659
We don't have to do this, Tony.


00:58:53.951 --> 00:58:55.619
You wanna be the War Machine,
take your shot.


00:58:55.702 --> 00:58:57.538
-Put it down!
-You gonna take a shot?


00:58:57.621 --> 00:58:58.872
-Put it down!
-No!


00:58:58.956 --> 00:59:00.415
-Drop it, Tony!
-Take it.


01:00:11.445 --> 01:00:13.864
Edwards Tower, this is Lieutenant
Colonel James Rhodes,


01:00:13.947 --> 01:00:17.159
inbound from three miles east
at 5,000 feet...

